/**
 * @page styleguide Style-Guide
 *
 * # Naming Conventions
 *
 * When making changes to the library, the naming conventions should be
 * followed. The most important naming conventions are listed below:
 * 
 * - Member variables are given the prefix "m_" and are written in "camelCase,"
 * regardless of whether the variable is "public," "protected," or "private".
 * @code 
 * uint8_t m_camelCase = 0;
 * @endcode
 *
 * - Global and local variables are written in "camelCase".
 * @code
 * uint16_t firstDevice = 0;
 * @endcode
 *
 * - Functions are written in "camelCase." They should begin with a verb
 * describing the function, followed by the object upon which the function
 * operates.
 * @code
 * void sendByte(uint8_t);
 * @endcode
 *
 * - Contants, constexpr and #define are written in "SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE"
 * @code
 * static constexpr uint16_t TIME_SLOT
 * @endcode
 *
 * - Classes, Enum-Names and Enum-Values are written in "PascalCase"
 * @code
 * enum FamilyCode : uint8_t {
 *      Ds18B20     = 0x28,
 *      Ds2438      = 0x26
 * };
 * @endcode
 */
